# Testing rules

## Coverage targets (M1)

| Layer | Target | Why |
|----|----|----|
| `packages/adapter-sdk/` | n/a (types only) | Pure types, nothing to execute |
| `packages/adapters/*/` | ≥80% line | Adapters are file-format parsers; bugs here are silent data loss |
| `packages/core/` | ≥80% line, ≥90% branch on `retrieval.ts` | Federation logic is where ranking bugs hide |
| `packages/cli/` | ≥70% line | Some glue is fine to leave to E2E |
| `packages/mcp/` (M1.1+) | ≥80% line | Same logic risk as core |
| `tests/e2e/` | every CLI command path | Smoke that the binary actually works |

## Test file location

- Adapter / core / mcp unit tests: **next to source** in `tests/` subdir of the package.
  - Example: `packages/adapters/claude-code/tests/scan.test.ts`
- End-to-end (spawning the CLI): `tests/e2e/<command>.test.ts`
- Integration (multiple adapters + core, no CLI): `tests/integration/<scenario>.test.ts`
- Shared fixtures: `tests/fixtures/<adapter-name>/`

## Required test types

### 1. Unit tests (per file)
Standard happy path + 1-2 edge cases.

### 2. Adapter conformance tests
For each adapter, the **mandatory four** (see `adapter-design.mdc`):
- `detect.test.ts`
- `scan.test.ts`
- `corrupt.test.ts`
- `denylist.test.ts`

### 3. CLI E2E tests
Every command in `packages/cli/src/commands/` MUST have an E2E test that:
- Spawns the actual `bin/omem` binary
- Runs against `tests/fixtures/` (NEVER against real `~/.claude`)
- Asserts exit code AND output schema (if `--json`)

### 4. Cross-platform tests
At least one E2E test runs on Windows in CI. Path-handling bugs are common and only show up there.

### 5. Snapshot tests (when output schema matters)
Any `--json` output has a snapshot test. Schema changes must be intentional.

## Anti-patterns

| Don't | Do |
|----|----|
| `expect(result).toBeTruthy()` | `expect(result.records).toHaveLength(3)` — assert specifics |
| Test that depends on `~/.claude` existing | Use `tests/fixtures/claude-code/valid.jsonl` |
| Test that prints to stdout in passing case | Tests are silent on green |
| Mock `fs` with a global override | Use `tests/fixtures/` and pass paths via the API |
| `.skip` or `.only` committed to main | Pre-commit lint catches; don't bypass |
| One giant `it("does everything", ...)` | One `it` per behavior |

## Running tests

```bash
bun test                              # all
bun test packages/adapters/cursor     # one package
bun test tests/e2e/scan.test.ts       # one file
bun test --coverage                   # with coverage report
bun test --watch                      # watch mode
```
